                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Well, this game's short description says it all: it's a short casual funny game, that will keep you occupied for ten minutes per day. \nAnd for its price (and the fact that it's bundled everywhere I think), it's worth it in my view.\nIts concept's very very basic and can be played both with your mouse or with a gamepad or such - you'll control a triangle with three sides colored of red, yellow and blue.\nPlatforms matching those colors will come your way, from the upper side of the screen like a retro arcade shooter (of course they won't shoot anything, they're colored platforms XD).\nYour mouse will work like in Tetris - left or right mouse button (or other gamepad controls) in order to rotate the main angle of your character, so that it will match the incoming platform.\nThat's it - there's a scoreboard on the upper left side of the screen and nothing else.\nA nice new age/relaxing soundtrack and some sound effects.\nThe game has no pause button, but it doesn't run in tray and I suggest you to play it windowed, so with a simple alt+tab pressing you'll pause everything, especially with your other hand controlling the mouse (really, there's no need of a joystick).\nFor what concerns controls anyways, since this game has been made with the Unity engine in the main menu you'll be able to change the controls (which are, for what concerns keyboard and mouse, originally binded to left and right mouse button and left and right CTRL key).\nI found anyways that playing with the mouse is the best way to get around.\nAfter you'll get your counter over 25 or 30 platforms hit, they'll start of course to pop up with more frequency - often one right after the other - so that you'll be forced to keep your reflexes ready and change in the right way your main triangle point.\nI mean, do you remember A and B in Tetris? When you used to rotate the L-shaped pieces? xD\nAfter 55 or 60 points, the platforms will easily overlap and you'll be required to be really responsive in order not to get hit - you don't have upgrades or lives, so that a wrong color encountering the non-matching platform is an instant game over.\nStill, despite being so minimalistic and simple, it's challenging and it's relaxing.. in my view, it's a nice way to spend some spare minutes of your day.\nThe fact that you can also remap your two controls is quite nice, if you find yourself not that great playing with your mouse or the pre-mapped CTRL keys.\nThe controls are super responsive and being so small and casual there are no problems of lag or bugs whatsoever. Of course, some skills will be needed if you wanna climb the leaderboards but really who cares, it's just for your entertainment.\nMore than ten minutes a day probably will annoy everyone, but taken as a casual logic game which will test some of your reflexes it's a nice deal, and I'd definitely suggest it for its low price to anyone who likes these games :)\nJust keep in mind that the whole game concept is based on a rotating triangle, three colors, and platforms with these colors coming your way from above.. so that you'll probably hardly reach more than the 100th one, and the game doesn't offer anything else.\nIf you like this kind of minimalistic/casual approach though, it's a nice game to have and it's well-realized overall :)",
